.TH STQR 1 "November 2026" "STQR" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
stqr \- distributed object storage daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B stqr
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
STQR serves object storage, its administrative dashboard and the native
WebSocket protocol on a shared HTTP listener. Administration uses the dashboard;
there are no administrative CLI subcommands. TLS is not provided; use an SSH
tunnel for remote administration.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --config " path"
YAML configuration. The Debian service uses /etc/stqr/stqr.yaml.
.TP
.BI --listen " address"
HTTP bind address (default :7419).
.TP
.BI --port " number"
Override the port while preserving the configured listen host.
.TP
.BI --name " name"
Node display name.
.TP
.BI --advertise " URL"
Contact address published to peers.
.TP
.BI --connect " URL"
First-contact helper for an existing cluster. Discovered peers remain authoritative.
.TP
.BI --data-dir " path"
Local data directory, resolved relative to the configuration directory.
.TP
.BI --volumes-dir " path"
Directory for file volumes, resolved relative to the data directory.
.TP
.BI --system-volume-bytes " bytes"
Initial admin-volume capacity (default 1048576); it grows on demand.
.TP
.BI --ram-bytes " bytes"
RAM-volume budget; zero uses available system RAM.
.TP
.BI --ramcache-bytes " bytes"
Reserved for the later read-cache implementation.
.TP
.BI --allow-subnet " CIDR,CIDR"
Allowed IPv4/IPv6 source networks. Default: loopback only. Empty allows all.
.TP
.B --version
Print software version and Git revision, then exit.
.TP
.B --help
Print available options.
.SH SIGNALS
SIGTERM and SIGINT perform SHORT shutdown: preserve data and ownership, inform
peers to wait for this node, and flush before exiting. Draining requires an
explicit administrative command.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/stqr/stqr.yaml
Node configuration and initial credentials; mode 0600. The daemon updates it.
.TP
.I /var/lib/stqr
Default data directory of the Debian service.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1)
.PP
/usr/share/doc/stqr/debian.md
